const e={toc:[{id:"why-the-order-of-services-matters",text:"Why the Order of Services Matters",level:2},{id:"hair-colour-after-keratin-colour-first-or-smoothing-first",text:"Hair Colour After Keratin: Colour First or Smoothing First?",level:2},{id:"why-many-stylists-colour-first",text:"Why many stylists colour first",level:3},{id:"when-the-order-might-change",text:"When the order might change",level:3},{id:"how-long-should-you-wait",text:"How Long Should You Wait?",level:2},{id:"colouring-hair-thats-already-smoothed",text:"Colouring Hair That's Already Smoothed",level:2},{id:"smoothing-hair-thats-already-coloured",text:"Smoothing Hair That's Already Coloured",level:2},{id:"planning-both-services-an-example",text:"Planning Both Services: An Example",level:2},{id:"protecting-hair-thats-coloured-and-smoothed",text:"Protecting Hair That's Coloured and Smoothed",level:2},{id:"use-the-right-shampoo",text:"Use the right shampoo",level:3},{id:"watch-the-water-temperature",text:"Watch the water temperature",level:3},{id:"always-use-heat-protectant",text:"Always use heat protectant",level:3},{id:"book-regular-hair-spas",text:"Book regular hair spas",level:3},{id:"protect-from-sun-and-chlorine",text:"Protect from sun and chlorine",level:3},{id:"henna-and-home-colour",text:"Henna and Home Colour",level:2},{id:"signs-your-hair-needs-a-break",text:"Signs Your Hair Needs a Break",level:2},{id:"what-to-tell-your-stylist",text:"What to Tell Your Stylist",level:2},{id:"keeping-both-results-looking-their-best",text:"Keeping Both Results Looking Their Best",level:2},{id:"common-mistakes",text:"Common Mistakes",level:2},{id:"plan-your-colour-and-smoothing-in-bangalore",text:"Plan Your Colour and Smoothing in Bangalore",level:2}],before:`<p>Smooth, frizz-free hair and a fresh new shade often go hand in hand. But if you&#39;ve recently had a smoothing treatment, or you&#39;re planning one, you might be wondering whether you can colour your hair too, and in what order. Getting <strong>hair colour after keratin</strong> or smoothening is usually possible. The key is planning the order and spacing of your services with your stylist.</p>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<p>This guide explains why the order matters, the general principles stylists follow, how to protect hair that&#39;s both coloured and smoothed, and what to tell your stylist at your consultation.</p>
</details>
<h2 id="why-the-order-of-services-matters">Why the Order of Services Matters</h2>
<p>Both colour and smoothing treatments work on your hair&#39;s structure. Done carelessly or too close together, they can:</p>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<ul>
<li>Affect how your colour looks or how long it lasts</li>
<li>Affect how your smoothing treatment looks and wears</li>
<li>Put extra stress on your hair, leaving it dry or fragile</li>
</ul>
<p>Planned well, you can enjoy both: smooth, manageable hair and colour you love.</p>
</details>
<h2 id="hair-colour-after-keratin-colour-first-or-smoothing-first">Hair Colour After Keratin: Colour First or Smoothing First?</h2>
<p>There&#39;s no single rule for everyone, but there are common principles.</p>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<h3 id="why-many-stylists-colour-first">Why many stylists colour first</h3>
<p>Many stylists prefer to colour first and smooth afterwards. Smoothing treatments can affect how fresh colour looks, so doing the colour first lets your stylist see the true shade before smoothing.</p>
<h3 id="when-the-order-might-change">When the order might change</h3>
<p>Your stylist may plan differently if:</p>
<ul>
<li>Your colour is just a root touch-up</li>
<li>Your hair has recently been smoothed and needs a break</li>
<li>You&#39;re making a big colour change that needs lightening</li>
<li>Your hair is already fragile from previous treatments</li>
</ul>
<p>The right order depends on your hair, your colour plans and your treatment. That&#39;s why a consultation matters.</p>
</details>
<h2 id="how-long-should-you-wait">How Long Should You Wait?</h2>
<p>Timing depends on the treatment, your hair&#39;s condition and the colour you want. Rather than guessing, tell your stylist exactly when you had your last colour or smoothing treatment. They&#39;ll advise how long to wait before the next service and plan the gap that&#39;s safest for your hair.</p>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<p>As a general habit:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Don&#39;t book colour and smoothing on the same visit</strong> unless your stylist recommends it.</li>
<li><strong>Leave time between services</strong> so your hair can recover.</li>
<li><strong>Plan ahead for events.</strong> If you have a wedding or big occasion, schedule both services well in advance.</li>
</ul>
</details>
<h2 id="colouring-hair-thats-already-smoothed">Colouring Hair That&#39;s Already Smoothed</h2>
<p>If you&#39;ve already had keratin, smoothening or straightening and now want colour:</p>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<ul>
<li><strong>Tell your stylist everything:</strong> what treatment you had, when, and any previous colour.</li>
<li><strong>Expect a condition check.</strong> Your stylist will look at how your hair feels before choosing a colour approach.</li>
<li><strong>Consider a gentler option.</strong> Ammonia-free colour may suit some clients who colour often.</li>
<li><strong>Add Olaplex.</strong> It helps protect and strengthen hair during colouring. At Xing, you can add an Olaplex top-up to any <a href="/services/global-hair-color">hair colour service</a>.</li>
</ul>
</details>
<h2 id="smoothing-hair-thats-already-coloured">Smoothing Hair That&#39;s Already Coloured</h2>
<p>If your hair is coloured and you want keratin, smoothening or another treatment:</p>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<ul>
<li><strong>Mention all colour,</strong> including highlights, balayage and any lightening.</li>
<li><strong>Lightened hair needs extra care.</strong> Highlights and balayage leave hair more porous and fragile.</li>
<li><strong>Your stylist may suggest a repair step first,</strong> such as an Olaplex Hair Spa, if your hair is weak.</li>
</ul>
<p>Our comparison of <a href="/blog/keratin-vs-smoothening-vs-straightening">keratin vs smoothening vs straightening</a> explains which smoothing treatment suits which hair.</p>
</details>
`,after:`<h2 id="planning-both-services-an-example">Planning Both Services: An Example</h2>
<p>Here&#39;s how a stylist might plan both, as a general illustration. Your own plan will depend on your hair:</p>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<ol>
<li><strong>Consultation:</strong> discuss your colour goals and smoothing goals together.</li>
<li><strong>Colour appointment:</strong> your new shade, with Olaplex if lightening is involved.</li>
<li><strong>Gap:</strong> time for your hair to settle, as advised by your stylist.</li>
<li><strong>Smoothing appointment:</strong> keratin, smoothening or another treatment.</li>
<li><strong>Maintenance:</strong> regular hair spas, root touch-ups and a colour-safe, sulphate-free routine.</li>
</ol>
</details>
<h2 id="protecting-hair-thats-coloured-and-smoothed">Protecting Hair That&#39;s Coloured and Smoothed</h2>
<p>Hair that has had both colour and smoothing needs gentle, consistent care.</p>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<h3 id="use-the-right-shampoo">Use the right shampoo</h3>
<p>A sulphate-free, colour-safe shampoo protects both your colour and your treatment. It&#39;s the most important product change you can make.</p>
<h3 id="watch-the-water-temperature">Watch the water temperature</h3>
<p>Wash with cool or lukewarm water. Hot water fades colour and wears smoothing treatments down faster.</p>
<h3 id="always-use-heat-protectant">Always use heat protectant</h3>
<p>Smooth hair needs less heat to style. Use a heat protectant every time and keep tools on a lower setting.</p>
<h3 id="book-regular-hair-spas">Book regular hair spas</h3>
<p>A <a href="/services/hair-spa">hair spa</a> every few weeks keeps coloured, smoothed hair soft and nourished. An Olaplex Hair Spa or Olaplex add-on helps if your hair has been lightened.</p>
<h3 id="protect-from-sun-and-chlorine">Protect from sun and chlorine</h3>
<p>Strong sun and chlorinated water can fade colour and dry out treated hair. Cover up and rinse after swimming.</p>
<p>Our <a href="/blog/keratin-aftercare-tips">keratin aftercare guide</a> and <a href="/blog/what-is-olaplex">Olaplex guide</a> cover these habits in more detail.</p>
</details>
<h2 id="henna-and-home-colour">Henna and Home Colour</h2>
<p>If you&#39;ve used henna or a box colour at home, tell your stylist before any salon colour or smoothing treatment. Home products can sit on the hair differently from salon colour and can affect how a new colour or treatment takes. Your stylist may want to check your hair first, or do a strand test, before going ahead.</p>
<h2 id="signs-your-hair-needs-a-break">Signs Your Hair Needs a Break</h2>
<p>Sometimes the kindest thing is to pause before the next chemical service. Watch for:</p>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<ul>
<li>Hair that feels rough, straw-like or stretchy when wet</li>
<li>Ends that split or snap easily</li>
<li>Colour that fades very quickly</li>
<li>A scalp that feels tender or irritated</li>
</ul>
<p>If you notice these, ask your stylist about a repair-focused hair spa, such as an Olaplex Hair Spa, before booking more colour or smoothing. Healthy hair holds colour better and responds better to smoothing treatments.</p>
</details>
<h2 id="what-to-tell-your-stylist">What to Tell Your Stylist</h2>
<p>Be as specific as you can at your consultation:</p>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<ul>
<li>Which smoothing treatment you had (keratin, smoothening, straightening, nanoplastia or another)</li>
<li>When you had it</li>
<li>Any colour, highlights, balayage or lightening, and when</li>
<li>Any home colour or henna</li>
<li>Any scalp sensitivity, allergies or pregnancy</li>
<li>The colour and finish you want next</li>
</ul>
<p>The more your stylist knows, the better they can plan both services safely.</p>
</details>
<h2 id="keeping-both-results-looking-their-best">Keeping Both Results Looking Their Best</h2>
<p>Once your colour and smoothing are done, the goal is to protect both. A colour-safe, sulphate-free shampoo does double duty, protecting your shade and your treatment. Wash with lukewarm water, use a heat protectant every time, and book a hair spa every few weeks. When your roots grow in, a root touch-up refreshes your colour without recolouring your smoothed lengths again. Your stylist will advise how to time it, so your colour and your smooth finish both stay fresh for as long as possible.</p>
<h2 id="common-mistakes">Common Mistakes</h2>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<ul>
<li><strong>Booking colour and smoothing back to back</strong> without talking to your stylist.</li>
<li><strong>Not mentioning previous treatments,</strong> especially home colour or henna.</li>
<li><strong>Going straight back to a regular shampoo</strong> after colour and smoothing.</li>
<li><strong>Skipping heat protection</strong> because styling is quicker.</li>
</ul>
</details>
<h2 id="plan-your-colour-and-smoothing-in-bangalore">Plan Your Colour and Smoothing in Bangalore</h2>
<p>You can usually enjoy both smooth hair and fresh colour. The key is planning the order and spacing with your stylist, protecting your hair with Olaplex and regular spas, and switching to gentle, colour-safe care at home.</p>
<details class="read-more"><summary>Read more</summary>
<p>Book a consultation for your <a href="/services/keratin-treatment">keratin or smoothening treatment</a> and colour together at Xing Premium Unisex Salon in Sarjapur Road, HSR Layout or Brookfield. Tell us your hair history on WhatsApp and we&#39;ll help you plan.</p>
</details>
`,takeaways:["You can usually colour hair that has had keratin or smoothening, but the order and spacing need planning.","Many stylists prefer to colour first and smooth afterwards, but your stylist will decide for your hair.","Always tell your stylist about every treatment and colour you've had, and when.","Olaplex and regular hair spas help protect hair that is both coloured and smoothed.","Use sulphate-free, colour-safe products to protect both the colour and the treatment."],faqs:[{q:"Can I colour my hair after a keratin treatment?",a:"Usually yes, but the timing matters. Tell your stylist when you had your keratin treatment, and they'll advise how long to wait and how to plan the colour so your hair stays healthy."},{q:"Should I colour before or after keratin?",a:"Many stylists prefer to colour first and smooth afterwards, as smoothing treatments can affect how fresh colour looks. Your stylist will recommend the best order for your hair and your goals."},{q:"Can I colour hair after smoothening or straightening?",a:"Often yes, but hair that has been smoothed or straightened needs gentle handling. Your stylist will check your hair's condition first and may suggest Olaplex or a gentler formula."},{q:"Will colour affect my keratin results?",a:"Colouring can affect how a smoothing treatment looks and wears, which is why planning the order of services matters. Discuss both treatments together at your consultation."}]};export{e as default};
